    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "68 Calderwood Road is an extended three-bedroom family home extending to approximately 128.6 sq. m. (1,384 sq. ft.), offering exceptional potential for a purchaser looking to create a home tailored to their own taste and requirements. While the property requires modernisation, having been vacant for over two years, qualifying for the government vacancy grant it provides a superb blank canvas with generous proportions and an excellent layout. Built in the early 1950s, Calderwood Road is one of Drumcondra's most established residential roads. Today it remains a highly regarded address, particularly with families seeking generous gardens, solid construction and easy access to the city centre. \r\n\r\nA welcoming entrance porch leads to a spacious reception hall with guest WC. To the front is a bright bay-window living room, while double doors connect through to the generous dining room, creating an ideal arrangement for both family living and entertaining. To the rear, the extended kitchen/breakfast room overlooks the large private rear garden and offers excellent scope to create a contemporary open-plan kitchen and family space, subject to the necessary planning.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, two of which are generous doubles, together with a family bathroom. The spacious landing further enhances the feeling of light throughout the first floor.\r\n\r\nOne of the property's standout features is its substantial rear garden, providing potential for further extension if desired, while still retaining excellent outdoor space. To the rear of the garden is a large block-built shed, offering excellent possibilities for conversion into a home office, gym or studio. To the front, there is valuable off-street parking.\r\n\r\nCalderwood Road is a mature and settled residential neighbourhood that has remained consistently popular with families for generations. Residents enjoy a superb range of amenities within easy reach, including an excellent selection of both primary and secondary schools. Nearby primary schools include St. Patrick's National School, St. Vincent de Paul National School and Corpus Christi National School, while well-regarded secondary schools such as Maryfield College, Dominican College Griffith Avenue, Ard Scoil Rís and St. Vincent's CBS are all within close proximity. Dublin City University is also nearby, together with Griffith Park and the National Botanic Gardens. Drumcondra Village offers an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, supermarkets and local shops. The area is exceptionally well connected, with Drumcondra Rail Station, numerous Dublin Bus routes and easy access to the M1, M50, Dublin Airport and the city centre, making it one of Dublin's most convenient residential locations."
      },
      {
